.TH TTPSCOPE 1 "October 2026" "TTPscope 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ttpscope \- terminal research and study client for MITRE ATT&CK
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ttpscope
.IR command " [arguments]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
TTPscope synchronizes the Enterprise ATT&CK STIX bundle and provides offline
search, relationship exploration, matrix rendering, personal notes, and an
interactive terminal interface.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sync
Download and validate the current Enterprise ATT&CK STIX bundle.
.TP
.BI import " FILE"
Validate and install a local STIX bundle.
.TP
.BI search " QUERY"
Search object identifiers, names, aliases, and descriptions.
.TP
.BI show " ID"
Show an ATT&CK object and its incoming and outgoing relationships.
.TP
.BI matrix " [--platform NAME]"
Render the Enterprise matrix, optionally filtered by platform.
.TP
.BI note " ID TEXT"
Append a timestamped Markdown research note.
.TP
.BI notes " ID"
Print notes associated with an object.
.TP
.B tui
Open the interactive ncurses browser.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ttpscope/enterprise-attack.json
Cached STIX dataset. Defaults to ~/.cache when XDG_CACHE_HOME is unset.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/ttpscope/notes/
Research notes. Defaults to ~/.local/share when XDG_DATA_HOME is unset.
